Implement user story AMSD-1820: [Mozio] - Promo code discount amount missing for return trip legs in Mozio dispatch data submitted for email confirmation

## Story Description
When a return trip ticket with a promo code is purchased, the Mozio email confirmation does not display the promo code discount amount for the return leg (and possibly the outbound leg). The root cause is in the dispatch construction or mapping pipeline: the discount data from the order's promo code is not being correctly attached to each dispatch's report.price.discount field for return-trip legs. This affects the data submitted to Mozio via MozioSubmitOrderPayload.dispatches[].report.price.discount, which Mozio uses to render the confirmation email.

## Acceptance Criteria
- When a return trip ticket with a promo code is purchased, the dispatch data submitted to Mozio includes a non-null report.price.discount (with amount and name) for the outbound leg.
- When a return trip ticket with a promo code is purchased, the dispatch data submitted to Mozio includes a non-null report.price.discount (with amount and name) for the return leg.
- When a single promo code is applied to a return trip order, both the outbound and return dispatches carry the correct discount amount (the total discount is appropriately split or duplicated per leg as per business rules).
- When line items share the same trip dates but have reversed fromStation/toStation (e.g., AJ→UN outbound, UN→AJ return), each dispatch's report.price.discount reflects the correct promo code amount for that leg without being dropped or zeroed.
- When no promo code has been applied to an order, report.price.discount is absent (undefined/null) for all dispatches in both one-way and return trips, and the Mozio submission payload contains no discount data for any dispatch.
- When a promo code discount calculation results in a zero-value discount for a leg, the discount field is either omitted or set to a zero-value amount without causing an error in dispatch mapping or email generation.
- The promo code identifier (name/label) is included alongside the discount amount in report.price.discount.name for each dispatch leg so Mozio can render which promo code was applied to which leg.
- When a return trip is dispatched, the fromStation and toStation values for each leg remain correctly assigned (outbound leg retains original direction, return leg retains swapped direction) regardless of whether a promo code discount is present on the order.
- When a one-way trip ticket with a promo code is purchased, the dispatch data submitted to Mozio includes a non-null report.price.discount (with amount and name) for the single leg — existing one-way promo code behavior is not regressed by the return-trip fix.
- When a promo code name/label contains special characters (e.g., hyphens, underscores, spaces, non-ASCII characters), the discount.name field in each dispatch's report.price.discount preserves those characters without truncation, encoding errors, or sanitization that alters the identifier.
- When an order's promo code data is partially present (e.g., discount amount exists but name/label is missing, or vice versa), the dispatch mapping does not throw an unhandled error and the dispatch data is submitted with whatever discount fields are available, defaulting missing sub-fields to a sensible value rather than dropping the entire discount object.





